All 15 tests pass now. Here's what was fixed:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission` now compares roles case-insensitively using `required.lower() in (role.lower() for role in user_roles)` (`src/auth.py:10`).
- `is_admin_or_owner` now uses `or` instead of `and` so that either being an admin OR matching the owner ID grants access (`src/auth.py:15`).

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__` no longer uses a mutable default argument (`dict[str, int] = {}`), which caused shared state across instances. Now accepts `None` and creates a fresh copy (`src/inventory.py:13`).
- `add` now accumulates stock (`self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`) instead of replacing it (`src/inventory.py:20`).
- `reserve` changed the boundary from `>=` to `>` so that reserving exactly the available amount is allowed (`src/inventory.py:28`).

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify` now lowercases alphanumeric characters during the loop (`src/text_utils.py:19`).
- Repeated separators are collapsed with `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)` instead of a single `replace("--", "-")` (`src/text_utils.py:24`).
- `truncate` now accounts for the suffix length: `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix` (`src/text_utils.py:34`).
